 (notes
  "NO-BUILD by the combined table: C1 INCONCLUSIVE, C2 FAIL (FAIL outranks). C1: LIVE (B 62.3 % of 1,250 Friday-pairs, G 82.2 pp); return short (median delta +0.139 vs delta 0.200, m_S 0.170; 3/5 positive: +0.171/-0.044/+0.208/+0.139/-0.166); drawdown miss (arm medians P 29.77 - S 25.94 = +3.83 pp > 3.0); concentration miss (trim-3 > 0 in 1/5). C2: LIVE (B 58.3 % of 2,279, G 74.5 pp); return FAIL (median -0.280, 1/5 positive: -0.424/+0.199/-0.049/-0.280/-0.293; delta = m_S 0.324); drawdown within (+1.51 pp); concentration 2/5. decide.sh arithmetic re-derived independently. #3597 CLOSE-AXIS: no clash (this read is not ESCALATE). CLASS: REJECT-as-default-but-legitimate-axis (keep-as-axis): Price_band_seeded stays default-off; no further confirmation cells without a new mechanism argument; not retirement-eligible; a two-cell K=5 read rejects prioritising the axis, not the mechanism. Attribution per the rule: the 26y gap belongs to top-3000 breadth (what C2 removed). WHY: #3595's +0.348 was a few cheap sub-top-1,000 names replicated across seeds. Positions in names ranked below 1,000 (top-3000 list in force at entry) carry +197.3 of #3595's +204.5 pooled points, positive in 5/5 seeds at every cut 500-2,000. MERC/WAL/DINO/REGN/ADMA were outside the top-1000 list on their decision dates; ATML was inside and is held by both arms of all C2 seeds. C2 lists are 4 % under $14 vs 13 % in C1; names P adds are under $14 14 % of the time vs 42 % (C1) / 40 % (#3595). Where the other arm's list is visible, C2's cut swaps net +1.0 pooled; the loss is cash (-39.0 decision-time; -37.5 both-placed, including AVGO 2013-09-10 fills rejected for cash in k1/k4) and the unresolved channel (-32.0; TSLA 2013-04-05 k0, +230 %). One-arm doublers P-S per seed -3/0/-1/-1/+1 (CERN's is a phantom) vs #3595 +2/+3/+2/+2/+2. C1 is #3595's 2013-26 half replayed: Seeded hashes seed|date|ticker and sizes are NAV fractions, so same-seed C1 positions equal #3595's from 2015-2019 (all ten arm-seeds by 2023); C1's delta per seed has the sign of #3595's 2013-26 increment in 5/5 (median +0.139 vs +0.151); the lean is ADMA 2023-08-18 (tie-cut lottery, P-only k0/k3, +300 %, 28.6 % of entry NAV) and SAGE 2017-12-01 (cash lottery, k0/k3); the DD miss is #3595's 2018-01-26 -> 2020-03-25 P episode. Expectation (#3597): ~84 funded re-draws per 26y ~ 1 doubler (0.10-0.18 log) at top-3000, about half of that in C1's 13.5 y, less on top-1000: under both cells' delta. DEFECTS: C2 S-k0 CERN-wein-739 phantom 2:1 split on 2013-07-01 (close already post-split, adjusted_close steps x2; the detector rescales a held position with no raw gap: #3109 class; NAV +9.88 % that day vs +0.68 % P-k0; ~+$283k, ~0.06 log; booked as two trade rows; no outcome change); V7/V13/V17 read td-full's committed short files (chain-w D1); cash.sh omits fill-time cash rejections (15-30 per C1 cell, 60-79 per C2 cell). FORWARD: stop on the price-order axis (both reads agree); nested sub-window cells on the parent's seeds re-measure the parent after re-sync (2-6 y here), so period cells must be disjoint; a top-1000 cell is the hard test for top-N-cut levers (cf. cap 40). Writeup: dev/experiments/price-band-confirm-2026-11-13/README.md Results."))
